HFCAST AND THE HFCAST ENGINE

The propagation engine is the HFcast engine by Jonathan McSweet,
https://github.com/jonathanmcsweet/hfcast-engine, used unmodified as a
library (Apache License 2.0). HFPredict builds it from a mirror pinned to
the commit of tag v2.14.0 (f9782529dcd2e40d67eba6725687c69124dab1c1).
Its own NOTICE travels with it and is reproduced in the app.

HFPredict is a rewrite of the HFcast app by Jonathan McSweet,
https://github.com/jonathanmcsweet/hfcast (Apache License 2.0), and keeps
its features and structure. Parts of HFPredict's core are translated from
HFcast's TypeScript into Rust and are therefore derived from it:

  - the empirical swing and spread correction, its storm widening and the
    map correction against daily-median lattices
    (shared/correct.ts, shared/correctMap.ts)
  - the coverage, patch and strip lattices (shared/coverageGrid.ts,
    shared/coveragePatch.ts, shared/shard.ts)
  - the direction survey (shared/survey.ts)
  - the mode requirements, band plan and antenna definition cards
    (shared/modes.ts, shared/bands.ts, shared/antenna.ts,
    mobile/src/data/antennaFile.ts)
  - quality buckets, NVIS reach, city search, coordinate parsing, the
    space weather now-cast and the ionosonde lookup (mobile/src/data/*)
  - the map projection and its geometry (mobile/src/data/projection.ts)

Changes made: translated to Rust, restructured into one library shared by
an Android and a GNOME app, and adapted where the platforms differ. The
numbers and thresholds are HFcast's, unchanged. Translations of the app's
text into German, Japanese and Arabic start from HFcast's.

The data files in core/data/ come from HFcast's repository:
cities.json (from the VOACAP distribution, NTIA/ITS) and land.json
(Natural Earth). ssn.json has the same shape and is regenerated from NOAA
by tools/update-ssn.py.


