DATA

Ionospheric and noise coefficients (compiled into the engine): CCIR
Reports 322 and 340, published by ITU-R Study Group 3,
https://github.com/ITU-R-Study-Group-3/ITU-R-HF ("free from any
copyright assertions" for implementers), and NTIA/ITS. See the engine's
NOTICE and docs/licence.md for the full breakdown.

City list: NTIA/ITS, from the VOACAP distribution (itshfbc/geocity).
Coastlines: Natural Earth, https://www.naturalearthdata.com/, public domain.
Time-zone boundaries: timezone-boundary-builder,
https://github.com/evansiroky/timezone-boundary-builder, built from
OpenStreetMap data, © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open
Database License (ODbL) 1.0; packed by tzf-rs / tzf-dist
(https://github.com/ringsaturn/tzf-rs, MIT).
Time-zone rules: the IANA tz database, public domain, bundled by jiff
(https://github.com/BurntSushi/jiff, MIT or Unlicense).
Sunspot numbers: NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center, public domain.


ONLINE SOURCES (optional, switchable off in Preferences)

Solar flux and K index: NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center,
https://www.swpc.noaa.gov/
Measured ionosonde soundings: UMass Lowell Global Ionosphere Radio
Observatory (GIRO), https://giro.uml.edu/
Place search: Open-Meteo, https://open-meteo.com/, data under CC BY 4.0.


